      "content": "it's more than just \"speculation\" to me. if they can infer neurological patterns like you said, that means they basically have a backdoor into our subconscious reactions. if i'm walking past a certain storefront or seeing a certain political ad and my gait or heart rate shifts, they know exactly how i'm feeling before i even realize it. it feels less like a \"technological evolution\" and more like a systematic way to monitor the population's mental state. don't you think it's suspicious how much they're pushing these high-spec sensors into everyday footwear without any real transparency?",
